> f(x: u32) = x*x + x
> g(x: u32) = (x*x + x) + 2147483648*(x*x + x)
> f2(x: u32) = (x*x + x) + 0
> g2(x: u32) = ((x*x + x) + 2147483648*(x*x + x)) + 0
> f1(x: u32) = (x*x + x) + 0
> equiv f g
f and g are equal on the domain of f (proved by algebra: the two sides differ by a polynomial in x that is 0 at every point mod 2^32, each coefficient in falling factorials times its factorials being a multiple of 2^32)
> equiv f2 g2
f2 and g2 are equal on the domain of f2 (proved by algebra: the two sides differ by a polynomial in x that is 0 at every point mod 2^32, each coefficient in falling factorials times its factorials being a multiple of 2^32)
> equiv f1 g
f1 and g are equal on the domain of f1 (proved by algebra: the two sides differ by a polynomial in x that is 0 at every point mod 2^32, each coefficient in falling factorials times its factorials being a multiple of 2^32)
> equiv f f2
f and f2 are equal on the domain of f (proved by algebra: both sides expand to one polynomial in x mod 2^32)
